# Milestone: v0.9.4 (originally drafted at M3; reactivated at Phase 5 Task 5.4)
# Covers: chunk that registers a periodic via every() keeps the periodic alive
#         across subsequent REPL lines; the body fires repeatedly so a
#         later-sampled count strictly exceeds an earlier one.
#
# Original M3 intent was "chunk does not quiesce until the watcher fires and
# settles".  Under the current REPL harness each input line is driven to
# quiescence before the next is read, so the multi-fire angle is asserted
# indirectly: Realm.fired sampled later is strictly greater than the snapshot
# taken between two pump-driving reads.  Counter approach (vs. echo) keeps
# the expected output deterministic — only nil / 0 / true appear.
#
# Mechanism: every(1us, body) registers a UPeriodic; urbi_step's sleep-queue
# drain wakes the body strand whose next_fire_us has elapsed.  The trailing
# 0; 0; reads pump enough urbi_step calls that Realm.fired grows past the
# captured snapshot before the comparison runs.

var fired = 0
every (1us) Realm.fired = Realm.fired + 1
var s = 0 ; s = Realm.fired ; nil
0
0
Realm.fired > s
[00000000] 0
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 0
[00000000] 0
[00000000] true
